# Low Water: the reckoning, shared by all three acts. Game director, 2026-10-21. Private.
# Design: design/DIRECTOR.md, pillar 4 (the lie Lamb lives). The engine side is
# game/engine/rules/reckoning.mjs: it adds to `gap` whenever Lamb acts against a conviction Lamb
# has inked, tells a lie that matters (lied.*), or breaks a promise (broke.<id> while said.<id>
# or promise.<id> is held), and sets the flags below so the script can quote the exact betrayal.
# Writers: never show these numbers. Gate lines on the flags and on `gap - owned`.
#   owning a gap in a confrontation:   {do: owned += 1; ...the cost, paid there and then}
#   denying it:                        {do: denied += 1}
# The open gap is `gap - owned`. Honesty about a bad belief costs nothing here; only the distance
# between what Lamb said and what Lamb did is counted.

@var gap
default: 0
about: How far Lamb's acts have gone from Lamb's professions (convictions inked, lies, promises). Counted by the engine.

@var owned
default: 0
about: How much of the gap Lamb has owned aloud, at a cost, in a confrontation.

@var denied
default: 0
about: How many times Lamb, faced with the gap, denied it.

@fact gap.fire
about: Lamb said some lamps have to go out, and then kept one lit for the people who own it.
@fact gap.wall
about: Lamb said Gullet looks after Gullet, and then took the stranger's side.
@fact gap.sea
about: Lamb said the sea belongs to nobody, and then stood on the wall.
@fact gap.jars
about: Lamb said leave the jars alone, and then lifted one.
@fact gap.ledger
about: Lamb said follow the money, and then hanged a man for his character.
@fact gap.checked
about: Lamb said nobody owns the truth, and then repeated the Lantern Man.
@fact gap.dry
about: Lamb said the assessor takes no side, and then took one, and called it the middle.
@fact gap.lied
about: Lamb has told a lie that somebody acted on.
@fact gap.promise
about: Lamb has broken a promise somebody heard.

# The costs are felt, never shown. Each modifier names its reason in the check's sum the way every
# other modifier does, in the town's words, never the system's.
@modifier mod.gap.heard
skill: condolence, chit
mod: -1
when: var.gap - var.owned >= 3
why: They have heard you say it both ways

@modifier mod.gap.easy
skill: pride
mod: 1
when: var.gap - var.owned >= 3
why: The story you tell about yourself is very comfortable

@modifier mod.gap.loud
skill: dark, undertow
mod: 1
when: var.gap - var.owned >= 5
why: The voices that know are louder now

@modifier mod.gap.denied
skill: condolence, formletter, hearsay
mod: -1
when: var.denied >= 2 & var.gap - var.owned >= 4
why: Nobody believes a man who will not look at himself

@modifier mod.gap.owned
skill: condolence
mod: 1
when: var.owned >= 2
why: You said it was yours. People remember that
